    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::size_t amplification_activation_threshold = CBOR_AMPLIFICATION_ACTIVATION_THRESHOLD_DEFAULT;
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::size_t maximum_amplification = CBOR_MAXIMUM_AMPLIFICATION_DEFAULT;
};
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
The error values of the library, their conversion to
\f[CR]std::error_code\f[R], and the limits of a build.
.SS cbor::error
Names the fault that a call returns in its
\f[CR]std::expected<T, cbor::error>\f[R].
Bad input never throws.
The first value is 1, so a \f[CR]std::error_code\f[R] from a
\f[CR]cbor::error\f[R] is always true as a \f[CR]bool\f[R].
A wrong use of the library is not an error value: it does not compile,
or it throws \f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.PP
